172 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 88 0 R
/E (With their general dead and ambush signals given, hidden Maratha forces then attacked Khan's stunned army in the valley below, resulting in a decisive Maratha victory. The battle is regarded as one of the turning points that established Shivaji as a serious power in the Deccan, rather than a regional nuisance to be easily put down.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
173 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 88 0 R
/E (In the years that followed, Pratapgad remained a significant Maratha stronghold. It eventually passed out of Maratha control after the Third Anglo-Maratha War in 1818, when the British took over most of the Maratha Confederacy's forts. Today it's preserved as a protected historical monument, with the tomb of Afzal Khan still standing at the base of the fort and a bronze equestrian statue of Chhatrapati Shivaji Maharaj unveiled by Jawaharlal Nehru in 1957 marking the upper fort as a site of national historical memory.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
